   7:     """
   8:     Grow each red control pixel upward through black space, sidestepping right under gray blockers.
   9: 
  10:     Input structure
  11:     - The background is black.
  12:     - Red pixels are control pixels on the bottom row.
  13:     - The only other foreground color is the obstacle color.
  14: 
  15:     Rule
  16:     - From each red control pixel, repeatedly try to move one cell upward.
  17:     - If the cell above is background, paint it red and continue from there.
  18:     - If the cell above is an obstacle, step one cell right on the current row
  19:       and paint that background cell red; if that right cell is unavailable or
  20:       not background, stop that path.
  21: 
  22:     Key insight
  23:     - The red output is not a set of fixed columns: each bottom control emits an
  24:       upward path whose turns are caused locally by gray cells directly above it.
  25:     """
  26:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  27:     assert g.ndim == 2 and g.size > 0, "expected a non-empty 2D grid"
  28:     height, width = map(int, g.shape)
